  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 220 °C. Rub the squash halves with olive oil and salt and roast cut-side down for 40 minutes, until tender. Cool.",
    "Scoop the flesh into a food processor with the feta, ¼ cup olive oil and 1 tbsp honey. Pulse, then blend while drizzling in the water until smooth.",
    "Fry the sage leaves in the remaining ¼ cup olive oil over medium heat until crisp, then drain on paper.",
    "Lower the heat, soften the chile in the oil for a minute or two, add the pecans for a few seconds, then stir in 2 tbsp honey and simmer until slightly thickened.",
    "Spread the dip in a shallow bowl, add black pepper, spoon the honey-pecan topping over and finish with the sage. Serve with toast or crackers."
  ]
